Data Analysis
🏆 Top Product by Units Sold

LEGO Bricks was the best-selling product by volume, with more than 2 million units sold during the analyzed period.

📈 Monthly Revenue Trend

Monthly revenue showed an overall upward trend throughout 2022, continuing into early 2023 and reaching its peak in March 2023. Revenue then declined gradually through September 2023, followed by a sharp drop in the final period.

🧸 Revenue by Product Category

Toys generated the highest revenue at approximately $5 million, significantly exceeding the other categories, which generated approximately $2.2–$2.7 million each.

💰 Profit by Product Category

Toys generated the highest total profit at slightly more than $1 million. Electronics ranked closely behind, also generating slightly more than $1 million in profit.

📊 Revenue vs. Profit by Category

Toys generated the highest revenue, exceeding $5 million, while also generating more than $1 million in profit.

Interestingly, Electronics generated only approximately $2.25 million in revenue but ranked close to Toys in total profit, indicating that revenue alone does not fully explain category profitability.

🌎 Top Cities by Revenue

Ciudad de México generated the highest revenue at approximately $1.65 million. Guadalajara and Monterrey followed, generating approximately $1.30 million and $1.26 million, respectively.

Summary

The analysis shows that Toys is the strongest category in terms of both revenue and total profit, while Electronics demonstrates relatively strong profitability despite generating substantially less revenue.

At the product level, LEGO Bricks was the highest-volume product, while at the geographic level, Ciudad de México generated the highest revenue among the analyzed cities.

These findings demonstrate the importance of analyzing both revenue and profitability, as categories with lower revenue can still generate comparatively strong profits.
